WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.760
Security detections are not one-time rules that remain useful forever.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.360
They depend on telemetry, environments, threat behavior, analyst workflows,

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.095
and business context.

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:12.280
Detection lifecycle management treats detections as living defensive assets.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.965
Each detection should have a purpose, owner, data source, expected behavior,

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:18.960
documentation, review process, and improvement path.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.065
Without lifecycle management, detections can become noisy, outdated, duplicated,

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:23.720
or ignored.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.275
A rule that once produced useful signal may lose value as systems, users,

00:00:27.275 --> 00:00:28.869
and threats change.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:32.750
The lifecycle mindset helps teams maintain a reliable portfolio of signals instead of a

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.600
growing folder of unmanaged rules.
